## 2026-07-23 - US-003

- Most of US-003's scope (the `alt` reflected string property, and
  `handleChange_alt` updating the preview `<img>` alt attribute and
  toggling the badge's `.has-alt` class) had already been implemented
  during US-001, per that entry's notes. The one remaining gap was
  the acceptance criterion that `image-input:change` include the
  current alt text in its detail -- it previously only emitted
  `{ file }`.
- Wrote a failing test first (`change event detail includes the
  current alt text`) asserting `image-input:change` detail has
  `alt: ''` before any alt text is set, and the current alt string
  after `el.alt` is set and a second file is selected. Confirmed it
  failed (`actual: undefined`) before the fix.
- Fix: `handleFileSelect` in `src/index.ts` now emits
  `{ detail: { file, alt: this.alt ?? '' } }` instead of
  `{ detail: { file } }`.
- Files changed: `src/index.ts`, `test/index.ts`,
  `specs/prd.json` (US-003 `passes: true`).
- Tests: 1 new tape test (3 assertions), full `npm test` (lint +
  build + typecheck + tape-run) passes with 25 total assertions.
- No browser verification step was listed in this story's acceptance
  criteria (unlike US-001/US-002), so none was performed.
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - Before implementing a story, check whether a prior story's notes
    already did part of the work "ahead of schedule" (see US-001's
    note about the `alt` property) -- grep the acceptance criteria
    against current source first to scope down to the real gap.
